; FILED: bignum divided by an INEXACT zero — NATIVE is the wrong side here.
; Inexactness is contagious, so this is IEEE-754 division: +inf.0.
; native -r : 0        (wrong — the bignum is dropped before the division)
; vm        : +inf.0   (correct)
; Native codegen is not VM-owned; filed so the divergence is recorded rather
; than "fixed" in the VM to match a native bug.
(display (/ (expt 2 100) 0.0))
(newline)
